{
  "title": "Sprengel's Deformity",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4038/sprengels-deformity",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 30 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sprengel's Deformity is a congenital condition characterized by a small and undescended scapula often associated with scapular winging and scapular hypoplasia.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with a high-riding, medially rotated, triangular-shaped scapula, with associated limitations in shoulder abduction and flexion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation in the absence of shoulder dysfunction. Operative management is indicated in the presence of severe cosmetic concerns or functional deformities (abduction < 110-120 degrees).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common congenital shoulder anomaly in children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male to female ratio 1:3",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "bilateral in 10-30% of cases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "scapular winging",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hypoplasia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "omovertebral connection between superior medial angle of scapula and **cervical spine** (30-50%)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "interruption of **embryonic** subclavian blood supply",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "at level of subclavian, internal thoracic or suprascapular artery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "in contrast, Poland syndrome is subclavian artery interruption proximal to internal thoracic and distal to vertebral artery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "associated diseases",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**Klippel-Feil (approximately 1/3 have Sprengel deformity)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "congenital scoliosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "upper extremity anomalies",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diastematomyelia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "kidney disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osteology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "scapula consists of",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "body",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "acromion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "coracoid process",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "glenoid",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Articulations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "AC joint and glenohumeral diarthrodial articulations of the scapula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Muscles",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "muscles that insert on medial border of scapula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "levator scapulae",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "rhomboids major and minor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "teres major",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small portion just proximal to inferior angle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "latissimus dorsi",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "small slip of origin at inferior angle",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often referred for evaluation of scoliosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "high riding medially rotated scapula",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "loss of long medial border",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "equilateral triangle like shape",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "shoulder abduction most limited due to loss of normal scapulothoracic motion and glenoid malpositioning",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "forward flexion limited as well",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "no severe cosmetic concerns or loss of shoulder function",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical correction",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe cosmetic concerns or functional deformities (abduction < 110-120 degrees)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "best to perform surgery from 3 to 8 yrs of age",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "risk of nerve impairment after the age of 8",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "pre-operative planning",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "MRI or CT to identify omovertebral bar",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "procedures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Woodward procedure**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "detachment and reattachment of medial parascapular muscles at spinous process origin to allow scapula to move inferiorly and rotate into more shoulder abduction",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "modified Woodward includes resection of superiormedial border of scapula in conjunction with surgical descent",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Schrock, Green procedure**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "extraperiosteal detachment of paraspinal muscles at the scapular insertion and reinsertion after inferior movement of scapula with traction cables",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Clavicle osteotomy**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "in conjunction with above procedures for severe deformity to avoid brachial plexus injury, performed before movement of scapula.",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Bony resection**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "extraperiosteal resection of proximal scapular prominence for cosmetic concerns, may be done with other procedures or alone",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Woodward and Green procedures can improve abduction by 40-50 degrees",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
